{"name":"Carmen Miranda","hex":"#903e2f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"carmen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of carman"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/carmen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carmen Miranda","blocks":[{"text":"Maria do Carmo Miranda da Cunha, known professionally as Carmen Miranda, was a Portuguese-born Brazilian singer, dancer, and actress. Nicknamed \"the Brazilian Bombshell,\" she was known for her signature fruit hat outfits that she wore in her American films."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Carmen_Miranda_in_That_Night_in_Rio_%281941%29.jpg/330px-Carmen_Miranda_in_That_Night_in_Rio_%281941%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmen_Miranda","wikidata":"Q121655"},{"title":"Carmen Miranda (volleyball)","blocks":[{"text":"Carmen Miranda is a Spanish former volleyball player who competed in the 1992 Summer Olympics."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmen_Miranda_(volleyball)","wikidata":"Q5043527"},{"title":"Carmen","blocks":[{"text":"Carmen is an opera in four acts by the French composer Georges Bizet. The libretto was written by Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy, based on the novella of the same title by Prosper Mérimée. The opera was first performed by the Opéra-Comique in Paris on 3 March 1875, where its breaking of conventions shocked and scandalised its first audiences. Bizet died suddenly after the 33rd performance, unaware that the work would achieve international acclaim within the following ten years. Carmen has since become one of the most popular and frequently performed operas in the classical canon; the \"Habanera\" and \"Seguidilla\" from act 1 and the \"Toreador Song\" from act 2 are among the best known of all operatic arias."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Prudent-Louis_Leray_-_Poster_for_the_premi%C3%A8re_of_Georges_Bizet%27s_Carmen.jpg/330px-Prudent-Louis_Leray_-_Poster_for_the_premi%C3%A8re_of_Georges_Bizet%27s_Carmen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmen","wikidata":"Q185968"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Travessa_do_Com%C3%A9rcio%2C_Rio.jpg/500px-Travessa_do_Com%C3%A9rcio%2C_Rio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Travessa_do_Com%C3%A9rcio%2C_Rio.jpg/500px-Travessa_do_Com%C3%A9rcio%2C_Rio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Travessa do Comércio in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil; Miranda lived at number 13 when she was young.[14]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATravessa_do_Com%C3%A9rcio%2C_Rio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Carmen_Miranda%2C1930.jpg/500px-Carmen_Miranda%2C1930.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Carmen_Miranda%2C1930.jpg/500px-Carmen_Miranda%2C1930.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Miranda in 1930","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarmen_Miranda%2C1930.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/Aloalocarnaval_1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/35/Aloalocarnaval_1936.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Poster for the 1936 Brazilian film, Hello, Hello, Carnival!","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAloalocarnaval_1936.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Abbott%2C_Costello_and_Carmen_Miranda.jpg/500px-Abbott%2C_Costello_and_Carmen_Miran